# The store listing lives in App Store Connect and not here. Everything asc keeps on
# disk is either a working file for one command or a local copy of what the store
# already holds, and both are shaped by that one store: keywords cut to its hundred
# characters, screenshots named by its display types. This repository is the base a
# build for any platform comes off, so a store's own schema does not belong in it.
# `asc metadata pull` fetches the listing whenever it is wanted, which is what makes
# the copy a derivative rather than the original.
.asc/
/metadata/
/screenshots/
